🔹 tnature (Transaction Nature)
Determine by applying the first matching rule below:

1. Route/Location Keyword Check (PRIMARY — use fuzzy/keyword matching, not exact phrase matching):
   - Scan the route/description text (from both the main invoice table AND the second-page material description) for the presence of the keywords KHARAGPUR, DHULAGARH, and HOWRAH — in any order, any spacing, any surrounding words (e.g., "KGP TO DHULAGARH TRANSPORT", "DHULAGARH-KHARAGPUR", "EX-KHARAGPUR TO HOWRAH" all count as matches). Do NOT require an exact string match against a fixed phrase.
   - If the route mentions KHARAGPUR and (DHULAGARH or HOWRAH) together, in either direction → "Interlock transfer"
   - Else if the route mentions DHULAGARH and some other place that is NOT Kharagpur/Howrah, with DHULAGARH as the origin → "Sales Related"
   - Else if the route mentions some other place that is NOT Kharagpur/Howrah as origin, going TO Dhulagarh or Kharagpur → "Purchase related"

2. Gatepass NO. prefix (FALLBACK ONLY — use this ONLY if step 1 found NONE of the keywords KHARAGPUR, DHULAGARH, or HOWRAH anywhere in the route/description text at all):
   - If gatepass_no starts with L1 / L2 → "Interlock transfer"
   - If gatepass_no starts with BS26 → "Purchase related"
   - If gatepass_no starts with LP / LK / LT → "Sales Related"

3. Else → null

IMPORTANT: Step 2 (gatepass fallback) must NEVER override Step 1. If KHARAGPUR, DHULAGARH, or HOWRAH appears anywhere in the route text (main table OR second-page description), the result MUST come from Step 1's route logic — regardless of what the gatepass_no prefix would otherwise suggest. A BS26-style gatepass prefix does not automatically mean "Purchase related" if the route text clearly indicates an interlock move between Kharagpur and Dhulagarh/Howrah.

(If multiple line items have different routes/gatepass prefixes, evaluate tnature per row logic first; if all rows agree, report a single invoice-level tnature; if rows disagree, return tnature as an array aligned to line_items instead of a single value.)

